---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import PageSection from "../components/PageSection.astro";
import PageSectionHeader from "../components/PageSectionHeader.astro";
import Prose from "../components/Prose.astro";
import Newsletter from "../components/Newsletter.astro";
import cover from "../content/landing/ruby/Cover.jpg";
import family from "../content/landing/ruby/Family.jpg";

// A testimonial is a block of its own here, so drop the margins meant for quotes inside running text.
// The quotes sit in a flex column, so they need the full column width instead of the 65ch of .prose.
const quote = "max-w-none [&>blockquote]:my-0!";

// Rendered width of the reading column: 36rem (about 684px) from 800px up, full width minus gutters below
const sizes = "(min-width: 800px) 684px, calc(100vw - 32px)";

const title = "Transform yourself from a friendly frontend engineer to a proper princess-life-saving skill builder";
const description =
  "Ruby's TimeShip - A story by @OlaHolstVea about skill building, time travel, and saving a princess.";

const testimonials = [
  {
    quote:
      "I'd be in prison in The Tower of London if it wasn't for Ruby's frontend skill building. She showed me how to build the right thing at the right time. And she did it with style.",
    name: "Lizabeth",
    role: "Princess of England and later Queen",
  },
  {
    quote:
      "Ruby is a wonderful opponent. Her frontend skills are annoyingly good. I almost caught her several times, but she always managed to build her way out of trouble.",
    name: 'Fulvia "The Fox" Renard',
    role: "Queen Mary's Super Spy",
  },
  {
    quote:
      "I wish I could turn back the clock and start my frontend skill building journey all over again. It was the most thrilling adventure of my life.",
    name: "Ruby Reckless",
    role: "Frontend Engineer on Ruby's TimeShip",
  },
  {
    quote:
      "Dammit, if it wasn't for Ruby's frontend skill building, I would have caught that treasonous sister of mine. Her builds were too fast, too good. I'll get her next time.",
    name: "Mary 1",
    role: "Her Murderous Majesty of Britannia And Badass Backend Engineer",
  },
  {
    quote:
      "Ruby Reckless, you finally convinced me that frontend skill building doesn't have to be boring. Your TimeShip adventure had me coding late into the night, and I loved every minute of it.",
    name: "Ola Vea",
    role: "Junior Frontend Engineer on POW!",
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} image={cover.src}>
  <SiteHeader />
  <main class="pb-12">
    <!-- Header Section -->
    <PageSection component="header">
      <PageSectionHeader badge="Ruby's TimeShip" title={title} hLevel={1} />

      <Image
        src={cover}
        alt="Ruby's TimeShip Cover: a collage"
        widths={[480, 720, 1200]}
        sizes={sizes}
        loading="eager"
        class="h-auto w-full border-2 border-ink"
      />

      <Newsletter formKey="timeship" cta="Send me the prolog now" tagline="Storytime" class="mt-6" />
    </PageSection>

    <!-- Main Content Section -->
    <PageSection>
      <Prose>
        <h2>Is your skill building stuck in the suck zone?</h2>
        <p>
          You know the suck zone. It's where you are when you start learning something new. You suck at it. You know you
          suck at it. And it feels like you'll never get out of it.
        </p>
        <p>You read the docs. You watch the tutorials. You copy the code. But you still suck.</p>
        <p>You need something more. You need a reason to build. A reason that matters.</p>

        <h2>Imagine that your sister might die...</h2>
        <p>
          Imagine that you are a frontend engineer in 1554. Imagine that your sister is locked up in the Tower of
          London. Imagine that if you don't build the right thing, at the right time, she will be executed.
        </p>
        <p>Would that get you out of the suck zone?</p>

        <h2>Join Ruby Reckless on her TimeShip</h2>
        <p>
          Ruby Reckless is a frontend engineer. She has a TimeShip. And she has a mission: save Princess Elizabeth from
          the Tower of London before Queen Mary has her executed.
        </p>
        <p>But Ruby can't do it alone. She needs you. She needs your frontend skills. And she needs them now.</p>

        <Image
          src={family}
          alt="The family, Ola, Lillian and Raae"
          widths={[480, 720, 1200]}
          sizes={sizes}
          loading="eager"
          class="border-2 border-ink"
        />

        <h2>How It Works</h2>
        <p>
          You sign up and receive the prolog of Ruby's TimeShip. Each chapter presents a new challenge that Ruby needs
          your help to solve. You build the solution using your frontend skills.
        </p>
        <p>The story motivates. The challenges teach. And before you know it, you're out of the suck zone.</p>
        <p><a href="#signup">Sign up now to get the prolog!</a></p>

        <h2>About the author</h2>
        <p>
          Ola Vea (@OlaHolstVea) is a junior frontend engineer, aspiring author, and the Cap'n of this pirate ship. He
          believes that the best way to learn is through story, and that the best stories are the ones where you are the
          hero.
        </p>
        <p>
          Together with Queen Raae and Pirate Princess Lillian (6), he creates adventures that turn learning into play.
        </p>

        <h2>What are you waiting for?</h2>
        <p>The TimeShip is ready. Ruby needs your help. Princess Elizabeth's life hangs in the balance.</p>
        <p><a href="#signup">Sign up now and get the prolog for free!</a></p>
      </Prose>
    </PageSection>

    <!-- Testimonial Section -->
    <PageSection>
      <PageSectionHeader title="Wait! Don't take my word for it..." />

      <div class="flex flex-col gap-8">
        <Prose class="max-w-none">
          <p>
            Here's what engineers back in 1554 said about getting motivated by Lillian (6
            &#x1F3F4;&#x200D;&#x2620;&#xFE0F;&#x1F478; ) and me:
          </p>
        </Prose>

        {
          testimonials.map((testimonial) => (
            <Prose class={quote}>
              <blockquote>
                <p>{testimonial.quote}</p>
                <cite>
                  <strong>{testimonial.name}</strong>
                  <br />
                  {testimonial.role}
                </cite>
              </blockquote>
            </Prose>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </PageSection>

    <!-- Final CTA Section -->
    <PageSection component="footer" id="signup">
      <PageSectionHeader title={title} />

      <Newsletter formKey="timeship" cta="Send me the prolog now" tagline="Storytime" />
    </PageSection>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
